description:
Grade a value that you will emit against the signed fact that your citation cites. The tool returns `matches`. When the value does not match, it also returns the `drift` between your value and the value in emem. This step catches a transcription error that would otherwise be a silent wrong number. A model can resolve a fact correctly and still type `0.2411` for `0.241103`. No other step in the loop sees this. Memory algebra: the `verify` operation (https://emem.dev/docs/model.html).

When to use: Call this immediately before you publish, log or pass on a value from an emem fact. Treat a false `matches` as a stop, not a warning. Use `value_verbatim` from resolve: quote that exact decimal string, then echo-verify the text you emitted. For a due-diligence or compliance record, this gives a signed check for each citation. Then you can state `every cited value was echo-verified`. The tool also accepts a bare cid, so a damaged citation still gets a grade.

Example arguments: {"token":"emem:fact:defi.zb572.xoso.zb1ec:4qj3l4mgh7ch5kvxmkqspjdl6y42oqhm42khh3gostccpixkbz5q","claimed_value":"-0.0522"}
